# Copy to `.env` in THIS directory — apps/merchant/.env.
#
# Expo reads `.env` from the app's own project root, the folder holding
# app.json. It does not walk up to the monorepo root, so a value placed in
# nelo/.env is never inlined and the app behaves as though it were absent.
#
# `EXPO_PUBLIC_` is the prefix Expo inlines into the client bundle. Everything
# named that way is public by definition: it ships inside the APK and every
# request already carries it. A Privy APP SECRET is a different thing entirely
# and belongs on a server, never in this file or anywhere in the bundle.
#
# These are read at BUNDLE time, so after changing them restart Metro with
# `npx expo start --dev-client --clear` and fully reload the app. A hot reload
# can keep serving the previous bundle. No new native build is needed — a
# development client loads its JS from Metro.

# Onboarding by phone number. Leave both empty and the app still runs: the
# phone route is simply not offered and Mobile Wallet Adapter carries it.
#
# The client ID is per-surface — create a client for the mobile app in the
# Privy dashboard, and add this build's Android application ID
# (com.nelo.merchant) and URL scheme (nelomerchant) to it, or requests from the
# app are refused even with a valid ID.
EXPO_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_PRIVY_CLIENT_ID=

# Where the till reads the chain. Defaults to https://api.devnet.solana.com,
# which rate-limits hard — fine for a quick check, not for a demo where a code
# stays on screen and polls every couple of seconds. Point it at an endpoint
# with a quota before showing this to anyone.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SOLANA_RPC_URL=
# Tried in order when the one above is down, slow or rate-limited, then the
# public endpoint last. Comma-separated. A second provider (a Helius key and a
# Triton or QuickNode one, say) is what makes this worth having.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SOLANA_RPC_FALLBACK_URLS=

# Nelo's relayer, which submits offline vouchers and pays the fees so the
# merchant needs no SOL and signs nothing. The public HTTPS URL of the tunnel in
# front of it, without a trailing slash, and the RELAY_TOKEN it was started
# with. See docs-site/operations/relay.mdx. Empty: a merchant with a connected
# wallet settles by signing and paying themselves; a Privy merchant cannot
# settle until this is set.
EXPO_PUBLIC_NELO_RELAY_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_NELO_RELAY_TOKEN=

# Nelo's settlement service (services/settle): cash-outs to a bank through
# paj.cash, and paj.cash's naira rate for the till. Its public URL and the
# SETTLE_TOKEN it was started with. Empty: no cash-out, and the till's rate
# stays fixed. paj.cash's own API key belongs on the server, never here.
EXPO_PUBLIC_NELO_SETTLE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_NELO_SETTLE_TOKEN=
